 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Descriptions and habits",
   "texto": [
    "The imperfect serves to describe the past (**A casa era grande**, the house was great) and to say what you were always doing (**Morava em Coimbra**, lived in Coimbra).",
    "It doesn't say when it started or when it ended. Just describe."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Terminations",
   "texto": [
    "In the verbs in **-ar**: **-ava** (falava, spoke). In the verbs in **-er** and **-ir**: **-ia** (eating, eating).",
    "Eu falava, your falavas, ele falava, we falavos, eles falavam. Eu comia, tu comias, ele comia, nos comos, eles comiam."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Unregular",
   "texto": [
    "**Ser** → **era** (era), **ter** → **tinha** (had), **ir** → **ia** (iba).",
    "Eye: **ia** (iba) comes from **ir** in imperfect. **Fui** (I was) is from the punctual past."
   ]
